WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.902
-Joel, since
you are a great actor

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.271
and you're quick on your feet,
I thought that it would be fun

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.040
if we put your movie knowledge
to the test.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.042
It is time for "A to Z."
Here we go.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:14.347
-♪ A to Z, A to Z ♪

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.815
-Now, here's how it'll work.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.516
You and I are going to
have a conversation

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:19.285
about our favorite movies,
but the catch

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.554
is that each time one of us
brings up a new one,

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.290
the title has to start with
the next letter of the alphabet.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.459
We'll go back and forth
and see if we can get

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.127
all the way from A to Z.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.428
Are you ready for this?

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:32.232
-It's the English alphabet,
right?

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.499
-[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:34.900
Well, tonight, we're using
the English alphabet.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.302
That's correct.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.737
I'll start off the conversation,

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:41.174
and then you'll start with the
letter "A" and your first movie.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.210
Joel, this summer,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.813
blockbusters, giant movies
coming out this summer.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.747
People are getting back
into the theaters.

00:00:48.747 --> 00:00:51.284
What are you excited to see
or what do you remember

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.219
your first blockbuster
that you saw?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.522
-Oh, I'm very excited
to see "Almost Famous II."

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.223
-[ Ding ]
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:58.223 --> 00:01:00.760
Yeah, that's a great --
I loved the first one, yeah.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.196
-Yeah, the manager in that
was incredible.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.165
-Yeah. He really was amazing.
Deserves an award.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.200
Thank you very much.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.804
I'm looking forward to the
reboot of "Bad News Bears"

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:13.873
just to see if I can --
-[ Ding ]

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.042
I mean, because I'm a big fan
of the old ones.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.311
-I get that. Do you ever --

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.013
Jimmy, I know that, like,
New York gets hot in the summer.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.882
Do you ever
just want to get away

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.084
to, like, a "Cold Comfort Farm."

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.620
-[ Ding ]
-Wow!

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.955
[ Laughs ]

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.457
-You ever seen "Diner"
with Mickey Rourke?

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.893
[ Ding ]

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.863
-Yeah, I've seen it. It's great.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.165
Tim Daly is in that, as well.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:42.535
Boy, that answer just went
"Every Which Way But Loose."

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.636
[ Ding ]

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.871
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:48.541
-Yeah, I almost belong
on a "Funny Farm."

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.209
[ Ding ]

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:52.244
-Boy, wouldn't that be
a "Great Muppet Caper."

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:53.613
[ Ding ]

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.682
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:58.517
-I remember "Great Muppet
Caper." I used to watch --

00:01:58.517 --> 00:01:59.953
It was a double feature.
That and

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.488
"Harry and the Hendersons"
in the same thing. It was good.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.790
[ Ding ]

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.191
-Hmm. Yeah.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.461
And the thing about Harry is
that he was, you know, real.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.662
It wasn't a puppet.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.497
Everyone knows
that Sasquatch is real,

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.167
but a lot of people, when
I get into that conversation,

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.435
we just have
"Irreconcilable Differences."

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.170
[ Ding ]

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.439
-Yeah, but do you ever see

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.108
the documentary about
the real dinosaurs.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.677
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.547
The theme park with, like,
real dinosaurs in it.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.049
It was a documentary.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.284
-Oh, yeah. "Jimmy Neutron"?

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:34.086
-No.

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:35.555
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.189
No. "Jurassic Park"
is what it was called.

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:39.391
It's a great documentary.
-You know, I don't know that,

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:41.794
and it's just nice
to be with you, Jimmy,

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.863
'cause you're a real
"King of Comedy."

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.230
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.934
-Thank you very much,
because I thought what we had

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.003
was "Lost in Translation,"
buddy.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.605
-Ohh.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.041
I didn't think because
I don't think it's lost at all.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.376
I just know
that "M is for Murder"!

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:58.911
[ Ding ]

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.246
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.681
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.883
-I want to tell you something,
and this is just between us.

00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:07.019
I've "Never Been Kissed."

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.221
[ Ding ]

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:11.924
-Oh. You should go to "Orlando."

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:14.460
-Are you sure?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.596
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.664
You sure?

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:23.770
-I swear you should go
to "Orlando," you "Oldboy."

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.970
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.840
-Okay. Yep.
-Okay.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.777
Well, whatever. I hope
you find some "Office Space."

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.711
-[ Ding ]
-Yeah, there you go!

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:34.480
Thank you. I will because -- -
-Those are all movies.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.081
I swear!
-No, I know they are.

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:39.518
Yeah, they are. You know
what I always think is funny?

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.220
I don't know if to say,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.091
"Pirates of the Cuh-ribby-in"
or "Pirates of the Cara-bee-in."

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.459
Isn't that weird?

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:50.896
-Uh, I think
it's "Cara-bee-ahny."

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:53.633
It's a very --
It's an unknown pronunciation.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:57.070
But, anyway.
[ Sighs ] This one's hard.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.338
-Yeah.

00:03:58.338 --> 00:04:00.673
-Okay, if I say the phrase,

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.374
"We are the mods,
we are the mods,

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:04.043
we are, we are,
we are the mods,"

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.377
do you know what
I am talking about?

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:06.845
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:10.249
You're talking about the band --
Pete Townsend and Roger Daltrey.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:11.450
-"Quadrophenia" is the movie!

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.419
-That's correct.
"Quadrophenia" is a good movie.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.553
[ Ding ]

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.322
Yes. It was almost as good
as "Road House."

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.856
[ Ding ]

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:21.527
-It was no "$cheme" that has
the dollar sign for the "S"

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.262
that you appeared in,
Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:25.031
[ Ding ]

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.565
You remember that.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:28.467
[ The Roots laughing ]

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.736
-You know, I don't remember that
because that was not what

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:33.272
the movie was called
when I filmed the movie.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.708
-Was it "Sheem" or was it --

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:38.177
-I was in a film.
My first film was called --

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:41.514
Yeah, "The $cheme" is what
they ended up calling it.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.683
That's very interesting.
It was --

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:47.386
-It was really good,
if you can find it.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:48.921
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.556
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.825
-It came out
and sank like the "Titanic."

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.493
It really did.

00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:58.063
-Aww. Well, they should've used
"U-571" to go get it.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:01.333
[ Ding ]

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.803
-Oh, uh, maybe they'll use
"Valkyrie" in the movie.

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:06.005
[ Ding ]

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.207
Tom Cruise
is in a lot of movies.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.009
-He is.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:13.612
-In the backlot of Universal,
they have a big --

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:15.881
a big thing that
you can drive through.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:18.417
-Right. That's right.
I've been there on that tour.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:19.786
"The Wicker Man" tour.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:21.954
-[ Ding ]
-That's not true.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.656
-I was thinking
"War of the Worlds,"

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.958
but, yes, "Wicker Man" tour
was the one, yes.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.461
-Oh.
-But it's like all space stuff.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.195
Some of it you would see in
the movie "The X-Files," maybe.

00:05:30.195 --> 00:05:31.631
[ Ding ]

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.899
-You mean "Fight the Future"?
"X-Files: Fight the Future"?

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:37.636
-That's correct.
Is that what it's called?

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:38.938
-I don't know.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.374
The Spanish translation
is "Y Tu Mama Tambien."

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.842
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.310
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.944
♪♪

00:05:45.944 --> 00:05:47.480
We're not done!

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.483
-Well, you left your mark
like "The Mark of Zorro."

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:55.621
Joel McHale!
"Crime Scene Kitchen."

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.290
"Crime Scene Kitchen" premieres

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.360
May 26th at 9:00 p.m.
You're so fun.

